Section 3 \'96 VISUAL & UX IMPROVEMENTS\
3.1 Mobile grid: 3 columns like Instagram 
\f2 \uc0\u55357 \u57313 
\f0 \
Your current gallery uses grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr)) with gap: 0. This works but on mobile it collapses to a single column because of the minmax(220px, \'85) minimum.\
To get a true 3-column grid on mobile (like Instagram), change the gallery CSS:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 css\
.gallery-grid \{\
  display: grid;\
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);\
  gap: 2px;\
\}\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Remove the minmax() and hard-code 3 columns. On very small screens this still works because the column width shrinks proportionally. Add a media query only if you want 2 columns on devices under 350px.\
